/* CLI */
"cli.usage" = "Usage:
  kidsafe-blocklist convert [--id ID] [--name NAME] [-o OUTPUT] FILE...
      Converts local lists (Adblock, hosts, domains) into a Privoxy .action file.
  kidsafe-blocklist update [--catalog CATALOG.json] [--conf-dir DIR] [--privoxy BINARY]
                           [--cache-dir DIR] [--dry-run] [--remove-legacy]
      Downloads the enabled lists, installs them into Privoxy, tests the configuration
      and rolls back on error.
  kidsafe-blocklist uninstall [--conf-dir DIR]
      Removes everything KidSafe added to Privoxy.
  kidsafe-blocklist lists [--catalog CATALOG.json]
  kidsafe-blocklist enable|disable ID [--catalog CATALOG.json] [--yes]
      Turns a list on or off (--yes: accept the warning for a large list).
  kidsafe-blocklist library
      Extra free lists that can be added.
  kidsafe-blocklist add-list [--catalog CATALOG.json] --from-library ID
  kidsafe-blocklist add-list [--catalog CATALOG.json] --name NAME --url https://… [--member PATH] [--id ID]
  kidsafe-blocklist add-list [--catalog CATALOG.json] --file FILE [--name NAME] [--id ID]
  kidsafe-blocklist remove-list ID [--catalog CATALOG.json]
      Adds or removes a custom list; it is installed on the next “update”.
  kidsafe-blocklist default-catalog
  kidsafe-blocklist pause | resume
      Pauses filtering (without deleting anything) or resumes it.
  kidsafe-blocklist block DOMAIN | allow DOMAIN
      Blocks or allows a domain (applied on the next “update”).

Without --catalog, the app's catalog is used (~/Library/Application Support/KidSafe/catalog.json).
Without --conf-dir, Privoxy is looked up in /usr/local/etc/privoxy, then /opt/homebrew/etc/privoxy.
Language: the system's, or KIDSAFE_LANG=fr|en.";
